## Requirements<a id="requirements"></a>

See the official documentation on how to [install Molecule](https://docs.ansible.com/projects/molecule/installation/#pip).



### Scenario `default`<a id="requirements-scenario-default"></a>

Additional requirements:

1. [Podman](https://podman.io/docs/installation).
2. The Molecule [plugin](https://github.com/ansible-community/molecule-plugins) `podman`:
   ```bash
   pip install "molecule" "molecule[podman]"
   ```
   or when using [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/):
   ```bash
   uv pip install "molecule" "molecule-plugins[podman]"
   ```



### Scenario `default_vm`<a id="requirements-scenario-default-vm"></a>

Additional requirements:

1. libvirt (QEMU/KVM driver and client), QEMU tooling and [passt](https://passt.top/):
   ```bash
   # Fedora
   sudo dnf install libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu libvirt-client qemu-kvm qemu-img passt

   # Debian, Ubuntu
   sudo apt install libvirt-daemon libvirt-clients qemu-system-x86 qemu-utils passt
   ```
   Please note that a user session (`qemu:///session`) needs no root privileges and no `libvirt` group membership.
2. Access to `/dev/kvm`. This works out of the box for locally logged-in (seated) users on Fedora, Debian and Ubuntu. Headless sessions (SSH, CI runners) on Debian and Ubuntu additionally need membership in the `kvm` group (`sudo usermod -aG kvm <user>`, then re-login).
3. The [`pycdlib`](https://pypi.org/project/pycdlib/) Python package in the Molecule virtual environment (used to build cloud-init NoCloud seed ISO images):
   ```bash
   pip install "pycdlib"
   ```
   or when using [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/):
   ```bash
   uv pip install "pycdlib"
   ```



### Scenario `ee`<a id="requirements-scenario-ee"></a>

Additional requirements:

1. [Podman](https://podman.io/docs/installation).
2. The Molecule [plugin](https://github.com/ansible-community/molecule-plugins) `podman`:
