## Usage<a id="usage"></a>

### Run tests<a id="usage-testing"></a>

#### Scenario `default`<a id="usage-testing-default"></a>

Tests the collection's resources against multiple OS platforms using Podman containers.

```bash
cd "/collection-root-dir"
export MOLECULE_GLOB="./{extensions/molecule,molecule}/*/molecule.yml"

# Test all defined platforms
# See the platforms key in molecule/<scenario>/molecule.yml for a list.
molecule test

# Test a single platform, use higher Ansible verbosity
molecule -vvvv test --platform-name="molecule-debian12"

# Keep instances after testing, clean up manually when done.
molecule test --destroy="never"
molecule test --platform-name="molecule-debian12" --destroy="never"
molecule list
molecule destroy
```



#### Scenario `default_vm`<a id="usage-testing-default-vm"></a>

Tests the collection's resources in QEMU/KVM virtual machines. This scenario exists for tests that containers cannot cover (kernel settings, nested virtualization, Podman in a VM, ...). The Podman based `default` scenario stays the everyday and CI workhorse; `default_vm` is opt-in and never runs on a plain `molecule test`.

```bash
cd "/collection-root-dir"
export MOLECULE_GLOB="./{extensions/molecule,molecule}/*/molecule.yml"

# Test a single platform (recommended; VMs are resource hungry)
molecule test -s default_vm --platform-name="molecule-fedora44"

# Test all active platforms
# See the platforms key in extensions/molecule/default_vm/molecule.yml for a list.
molecule test -s default_vm

# Keep instances after testing for debugging, clean up manually when done
molecule test -s default_vm --platform-name="molecule-fedora44" --destroy="never"
molecule login -s default_vm --host="molecule-fedora44"
molecule destroy -s default_vm
```

A resource guard fails the `create` step early when the sum of the requested instance memory (plus a host reserve) exceeds the available memory or when the image cache disk space runs low, pointing to `--platform-name` as the way out. Environment variables of this scenario:

| Variable                       | Default                                    | Purpose                                                        |
|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `MOLECULE_VM_LIBVIRT_URI`      | `qemu:///session`                          | libvirt connection URI                                         |
| `MOLECULE_VM_CACHE_DIR`        | `~/.cache/ansible-molecule-libvirt/images` | cloud image cache directory                                    |
| `MOLECULE_VM_REFRESH_IMAGES`   | (unset)                                    | set to `1` to force re-downloading the cached cloud images     |
| `MOLECULE_VM_IGNORE_RESOURCES` | (unset)                                    | set to `1` to skip the memory / disk space resource guard      |

The scenario downloads vendor cloud images (qcow2, several hundred MiB each) on first use and caches them at `~/.cache/ansible-molecule-libvirt/images` (override with the `MOLECULE_VM_CACHE_DIR` environment variable). The cache is safe to delete at any time, images are re-downloaded on demand.

Debugging hints if an instance does not come up:

- Boot console log: `~/.cache/molecule/<collection>/default_vm/vm/<name>/console.log`
- Domain states: `virsh --connect 'qemu:///session' list --all`
- Guest IP via the guest agent: `virsh --connect 'qemu:///session' domifaddr '<name>' --source agent`



#### Scenario `ee`<a id="usage-testing-ee"></a>

Tests that the collection can be included in an [Ansible Execution Environment (EE)](https://docs.ansible.com/projects/ansible/latest/getting_started_ee/i) built with [`ansible-builder`](https://docs.ansible.com/projects/builder/en/latest/).

```bash
cd "/collection-root-dir"
export MOLECULE_GLOB="./{extensions/molecule,molecule}/*/molecule.yml"

# Test: create collection artifact and EE image, verify inclusion in the EE
molecule test --scenario "ee"
```



